lines=['# Full guide audit - 10 October 2026','', 'Version 1.6.0. Reference: the Dark Souls II Wikidot guide, covering original DSII, Scholar of the First Sin and DLC. Wikipedia itself is not an item/stat database. No unmatched names remain in the specific roster indexes checked below. This establishes named roster coverage; it does not certify every placement, enemy variant, dialogue, statistic, quest step or image identity.','', '## Filters and sorting','', '- Armor: sets, head, chest, hands/gloves, legs; physical/elemental defenses, poison, bleed, petrification, curse, poise and weight. Choose +0 or maximum normal reinforcement. Set totals require verified values for every listed piece; partial sets sort as unknown.', '- Weapons: type, attack element, scaling channel, status buildup, weight and name. Scaling grades rank S, A, B, C, D, E. Attack numbers are base attack before attribute bonuses, with separate +0 and maximum normal reinforcement modes.', '- Items: type and consumable soul value. Enemies/bosses: area, name, HP and soul rewards, with known weakness filters for enemies. Areas: region/name/bonfire count. NPCs: character/summon versus lore figure and name.', '- Every filterable catalog has category search, a result count, an explicit empty state and Reset. Selections persist through detail navigation, Back and refresh. Unverified numeric values sort last in either direction.', '', '## Repairs made','', '- Added 88 missing spells: 25 sorceries, 18 hexes, 20 pyromancies and 25 miracles. All 106 indexed spells have local entries with uses, requirements, attunement slots and acquisition information.', '- Added 46 named enemy/invader entries, 15 characters/summons, the missing Leather Set and 36 ring variants. There are now 120 distinct ring entries.', '- Added missing armor slot labels and source-backed aliases for transparent Aurous pieces, the Forlorn chest piece and crown names.', '- Moved five friendly summons from Enemies into NPCs, preserving old routes and favorites. Reclassified two item overview headings as local guide articles and removed a duplicate armor item.', '- Corrected all nine covenant rank tables, including joining rewards, and added joining instructions.', '- Replaced unsupported enemy HP/soul numbers with published location/intensity profiles. Removed unsupported drop percentages and unverified weakness/immunity claims. Added only explicitly sourced damage multipliers, resistance categories and immunity statements.', '- Corrected Faraam weight values with the source table\'s decimal commas and completed the Wanderer Manchette maximum defenses. A duplicated Dragonslayer Greatbow +1 source row is handled without replacing the actual reinforced row with a mislabeled baseline row.', '- Filled acquisition information for 13 reinforcement/infusion materials. All 441 items now have descriptions, uses and acquisition information.', f'- Downloaded and decoded {repairs["image_success"]} source-associated images. All runtime data, fonts and images remain bundled locally.', '', '## Reference roster coverage','', '| Wiki index | Names checked | Unmatched |','|---|---:|---:|']
for n,r in rosters.items():lines.append(f'| [{n}]({BASE}/{n.removeprefix("armor-") if n in ["armor-head","armor-chest","armor-hands","armor-legs"] else "armor" if n=="armor-sets" else n}) | {r["compared"]} | {len(r["missing"])} |')
lines+=['','Index counts overlap: weapons/shields/tools, NPCs/enemies and alternative names can appear more than once. Armor counts include variants; published unused pieces are excluded from the normal app listing and retained as labelled direct entries.','', '## Verification evidence','',f'- {len(list((A/"fresh-sources").glob("*.html")))} local source snapshots are available. The initial refresh downloaded 1,232 pages without failures; follow-up pages cover additional missing entries.',f'- {facts["fields_checked"]:,} supported weapon/armor field groups match the refreshed source tables, with {len(facts["mismatches"])} mismatches remaining in that comparison. Groups include requirements, scaling, base attack, handling, normal reinforcement attack/scaling rows, and baseline/maximum armor defenses. This is a comparison of supported table layouts, not certification of all prose or unsupported source tables.', f'- {catalog["local_images_checked"]:,} distinct local images/icons pass existence and decoding checks; {len(catalog["broken_local_assets"])} broken local references.',f'- {local["rendered"]:,} detail pages and {local["links"]:,} generated internal links pass the whole-catalog check. No external requests, runtime errors, HTTP failures or content-security errors were observed.',f'- {filters["passed"]} filter checks, {len(interactions["passed"])} navigation/storage checks and {len(details["checks"])} mechanics/mobile checks pass.', '- The rapid full-catalog browser sweep serves real bundled asset bytes from disk to avoid flooding the local development server; initial loading, deep-link refresh and navigation still use the local HTTP server.', '', '## Remaining verification and content gaps','', f'- {len(legacy)} legacy enemy names remain unreconciled with the canonical source roster. They are visibly labelled, and unsupported stats are omitted. They may be aliases, NPCs or distinct variants; no identity is guessed.', f'- {len(generic)} entries use explicitly labelled generic artwork: 19 exact item icons and 3 enemy pictures. Some original artwork has not been visually compared with the game; decoding alone does not prove identity.', '- There are 78 individually described bonfires, but only two verified location screenshots. The remaining 76 screenshots are absent.', '- The quest tracker contains five questlines. It is not yet an exhaustive walkthrough of every NPC event and condition.', '- Original/Scholar placements and all NG/NG+ variants do not yet have complete separate profiles. Sourced location and intensity differences are shown where available.', f'- {len(facts["unverified"])} weapon verification groups need special handling or lack published reinforcement rows, listed below. Fists and non-reinforceable tools are not treated as normal upgrade paths.', '- Two alternate Prisoner designs lack fully assigned individual defense tables. Unused or identity-unverified legacy armor stays outside the normal list.', '- Spell cast counts and effects can depend on attunement, catalysts, character stats and equipment. Published mechanics notes are included; the app does not simulate every modifier.', '- The character builder and blacksmith expansion remain the next separate work item; this change does not certify infusions or extrapolated attack-rating subtotals.', '', '### Legacy enemy names to reconcile','']
